# Strigiformes

Strigiformes is the order of owls, nocturnal predators split between the barn
owls of [[tytonidae]] and the typical owls of [[strigidae]]. Almost every
species is abroad only after dark, preying on rodents it locates in deep gloom
by sound. The flight feathers carry a velvety pile and a comb-like fringe that
damp the wingbeat to nothing, so a rodent hears no approach. Prey is seized in
the talons and swallowed whole, the fur and bone cast up afterwards as a pellet.
